artifact.self_contained_problem:
A trisection of a closed connected oriented smooth 4-manifold $M$ is a decomposition $M = X_1 \cup X_2 \cup X_3$ such that:
(i) each $X_i$ is a 4-dimensional handlebody, i.e. diffeomorphic to a boundary connected sum $\natural_{k_i}(S^1 \times D^3)$ for some integer $k_i \ge 0$ (the case $k_i = 0$ being the 4-disk $D^4$);
(ii) the pairwise intersections $X_i \cap X_j$ ($i \ne j$) are 3-dimensional handlebodies;
(iii) the triple intersection $\Sigma = X_1 \cap X_2 \cap X_3$ is a closed orientable surface, called the central surface of the trisection.
The genus of the piece $X_i$ is the integer $k_i$ above.

Question: Does every closed simply-connected smooth 4-manifold admit a trisection in which at least one of the three 4-dimensional pieces $X_i$ has genus $0$ (equivalently, is diffeomorphic to the 4-disk $D^4$)?

